---
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import { execution, commandOutput, stages } from './model';
import './archive.css';
---
<div data-archive-lab>
  <section class="al-recorded" aria-labelledby="al-proof-title">
    <div class="al-section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">01 / Actual CLI execution, recorded</p><h2 id="al-proof-title">Rebuild the index<br /> <em>from its manifests.</em></h2></div><p>The unchanged Photo Archive CLI staged these originals, verified them, and rebuilt its index after that disposable file was removed. These controls select the saved evidence.</p></div>
    <div class="al-stage" data-archive-stage="initial">
      <article class="al-canonical"><header><h3><Icon name="archive" /> The canonical archive</h3><span class="al-pill">Preserved throughout</span></header><div class="al-fixtures">{execution.fixtures.map(fixture=><figure><a href={fixture.src} download={fixture.download} aria-label={`Download ${fixture.name} synthetic PNG`}><img src={fixture.src} width={fixture.width} height={fixture.height} alt={`Generated geometric color study: ${fixture.name}`} /></a><figcaption><strong>{fixture.name}</strong><span>{fixture.bytes.toLocaleString('en')} bytes</span></figcaption></figure>)}</div><div class="al-ledger"><span aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="image" /></span><div><strong>Originals + manifests + event ledgers</strong><p>Each manifest records the original’s size and SHA-256. The supplied metadata JSON is retained as another hashed resource.</p></div></div><footer><span><Icon name="check" /> All canonical hashes match</span><span>13 files checked</span></footer></article>
      <div class="al-stage-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="arrow-right" /></div>
      <article class="al-index"><header><h3>The derived index</h3><span class="al-index-file" data-index-file>Present</span></header><div class="al-index-body"><p class="al-index-name"><Icon name="corner-box" /> archive.sqlite</p><div class="al-counts"><p><strong data-index-assets>3</strong><span>asset rows</span></p><p><strong data-index-resources>6</strong><span>resource rows</span></p><p><strong data-index-integrity>ok</strong><span>integrity check</span></p></div><p class="al-index-note" data-index-note>{stages[0].note}</p><fieldset class="al-replay-controls" data-replay-controls disabled><legend class="al-sr-only">Select recorded archive step</legend>{stages.map((stage,i)=><button type="button" data-recorded-step={i} aria-pressed={i===0}>{stage.label}</button>)}</fieldset><p class="al-replay-disclosure">Recorded evidence. These controls execute no commands.</p></div></article>
    </div>
    <p class="al-stage-status" data-stage-status role="status">Initial index: 3 assets, 6 resources, SQLite integrity ok.</p>
    <div class="al-output"><div><span data-output-label>Actual command output</span><span>Data-root paths shortened to $DEMO_ROOT</span></div><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Recorded CLI output" data-command-output>{commandOutput('08-initial-index') + '\n\n' + commandOutput('06-verify')}</pre></div>
    <div class="al-proof-strip"><p><Icon name="check" /><span><strong>3 original PNGs</strong>Same sizes and SHA-256 hashes</span></p><p><Icon name="check" /><span><strong>13 canonical files</strong>Byte-identical before and after</span></p><p><Icon name="check" /><span><strong>Identical database rows</strong>Assets, resources and identities</span></p></div>
  </section>

  <section class="al-check" aria-labelledby="al-check-title" data-check-state="idle">
    <div class="al-section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / A separate check, in your browser</p><h2 id="al-check-title">Try the<br /><em>byte comparison.</em></h2></div><div><p>Fetch the three tiny synthetic PNGs and calculate their SHA-256 hashes locally with Web Crypto. Compare your results with the recorded originals.</p><p class="al-check-boundary">This browser illustration is separate from the CLI run above. It has no archive backend, uploads or saved browser state.</p></div></div>
    <fieldset class="al-check-controls" data-check-controls disabled><legend class="al-sr-only">Local synthetic-file verification</legend><button type="button" class="al-primary" data-verify><span data-verify-label>Verify three originals</span><Icon name="arrow-right" /></button><button type="button" data-change disabled>Change one copied byte</button></fieldset>
    <p class="al-local-status" data-local-status role="status">The recorded hashes are below. Enable JavaScript to calculate and compare hashes in this browser.</p>
    <div class="al-file-checks">{execution.fixtures.map((fixture,i)=><article class="al-file-check" data-file-check={i}><div class="al-file-head"><h3>{fixture.name}</h3><span data-file-result>Not checked here</span></div><p class="al-file-detail">{fixture.bytes.toLocaleString('en')} bytes · generated PNG · <a href={fixture.src} download={fixture.download}>Download original <Icon name="arrow-down" /></a></p><details><summary>Inspect the SHA-256 comparison</summary><dl><dt>Recorded original</dt><dd><code>{fixture.sha256}</code></dd><dt>Calculated in this browser</dt><dd><code data-local-hash>Not calculated</code></dd></dl></details></article>)}</div>
    <p class="al-memory-note"><Icon name="corner-box" /> Changing a copied byte affects one temporary array in memory. The hosted PNG, your download and the original archive evidence stay unchanged.</p>
    <noscript><p class="al-noscript">The full recorded proof, hashes, downloads and transcript are available without JavaScript. The replay and local hash calculation need JavaScript.</p></noscript>
  </section>

  <section class="al-receipt" aria-labelledby="al-receipt-title"><div class="al-section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">03 / Source, hashes and scope</p><h2 id="al-receipt-title">Follow the<br /><em>recorded evidence.</em></h2></div><a class="text-link" href="/media/archive/receipt.json" download>Download the public receipt <span aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="arrow-down" /></span></a></div>
    <dl class="al-facts"><div><dt>Recorded</dt><dd>15 October 2026</dd></div><div><dt>Source revision</dt><dd><code>{execution.sourceRevision}</code></dd></div><div><dt>Resources</dt><dd>3 originals + 3 metadata files = 6</dd></div><div><dt>SQLite before / after</dt><dd>3 assets · 6 resources · integrity ok</dd></div></dl>
    <details class="al-detail"><summary>Read every CLI command and its recorded result</summary><p>The actual Typer CLI ran through a guarded Python launcher. Commands below use its <code>photo-archive</code> entrypoint name. Only the disposable data-root prefix is replaced with <code>$DEMO_ROOT</code>. Refusal messages are labeled excerpts; full private tracebacks are omitted.</p><ol class="al-invocations">{execution.commands.map(command=><li><div><span>Exit {command.exitCode}</span><span>{command.durationSeconds.toFixed(3)} seconds</span></div><pre tabindex="0" aria-label={`Recorded command ${command.id}`}>{'$ ' + command.command + (command.stdout ? '\n' + command.stdout.trimEnd() : '') + (command.stderrExcerpt ? '\n[stderr excerpt] ' + command.stderrExcerpt : '')}</pre></li>)}</ol><p>Between the initial and rebuilt index, the guarded driver removed only <code>$DEMO_ROOT/state/archive.sqlite</code>. Its recorded file identity and both database snapshots are in the public receipt.</p><a class="text-link" href="/media/archive/transcript.txt">Open the text transcript <span aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></span></a></details>
    <details class="al-detail"><summary>Inspect source hashes and the canonical boundary</summary><p>The four named source files below match the committed revision and retain the same hashes after the run. Six focused, existing source tests passed: staging success and overwrite refusal, sentinel enforcement, resource verification and corruption rejection, and complete index reconstruction.</p><div class="al-source-hashes">{Object.entries(execution.sourceFiles).map(([path,file])=><div><strong>{path}</strong><code>{file.sha256}</code></div>)}</div><p>The 13 canonical files are three PNG originals, three retained metadata JSONs, three manifests, three event ledgers and one volume sentinel. Every file’s size and SHA-256 match before and after. The public receipt includes both complete file-identity snapshots and both index row sets.</p></details>
    <details class="al-detail"><summary>What the isolated run substituted and refused</summary><p>The original source checkout remained unchanged. An explicit allowlist of committed code and narrow tests ran in an isolated copy. Three code-generated PNGs and minimal invented metadata replaced all real library inputs. The original home directories and real-volume paths were hidden; the network namespace was isolated. No Photos API, production catalog, archive server, model or enrichment operation ran.</p><p>Initializing the existing volume returned exit 1 without changing it. A positional index-destination sample returned exit 2 without creating a database; the successful commands use <code>--destination</code>. Staging retains a metadata JSON as a second resource, so three originals correctly yield six total resource rows. These are observations from the unchanged source.</p><p>Two test setup attempts encountered the sandbox’s read-only device restriction; disabling pytest capture and logging resolved them. The same six source tests then passed. Full private setup and failure receipts are retained outside this public exhibit.</p></details>
    <details class="al-detail al-recording"><summary>Watch the recorded prototype replay · 18 seconds</summary><p>This film records the private static prototype replaying the completed run’s evidence. The CLI commands had already finished. The display pacing is editorial; the film is not live CLI footage.</p><figure><video controls playsinline preload="none" poster="/media/archive/replay-poster.png" aria-label="Recorded static prototype replay of Photo Archive evidence" aria-describedby="al-film-caption"><source src="/media/archive/recorded-replay.mp4" type="video/mp4" /><track kind="captions" src="/media/archive/recorded-replay.vtt" srclang="en" label="English" default />Your browser does not support video. <a href="/media/archive/recorded-replay.mp4">Download the replay.</a></video><figcaption id="al-film-caption">A continuous browser recording of the earlier private prototype. It shows three saved states: initial index, disposable index removed, and rebuilt index. All images are generated fixtures. <a href="/media/archive/recorded-replay.vtt">Read the captions.</a></figcaption></figure></details>
  </section>
</div>
<script>import './controller';</script>
